<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW-READY-M8>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW-READY-M8" ;
  triage:title "Minor bundle: unescaped LIKE wildcard, bootstrap AlreadyInstalled fragility, silent OnceLock re-attach with no flush-thread stop signal, brittle queue-full string match" ;
  triage:description "fenix reviewer-A (01M1S6XV64XHNGSP00NWXK26RQ), quality-mgr confirmed (a) and (c) by direct source read; (b) confirmed by reading daemon_observability.rs:94-99; (d) accepted on citation. (a) crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/diagnostic_timeline.rs:92 `component LIKE (?4 || '%')` has no ESCAPE clause, so a component value containing %/_ behaves as a wildcard, not a literal (bounded by 20k/1000 caps, not a DoS, but incorrect filtering). (b) crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/daemon_observability.rs:94-99 hard-fails bootstrap if a global tracing subscriber is already installed (AlreadyInstalled -> bootstrap error); not reachable today since nothing else installs a subscriber first, fragility only. (c) crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/diagnostic_timeline.rs:30,65-66 `let _ = X.set(...)` silently discards a failed re-attach on ACTIVE_TIMELINE/ACTIVE_COUNTERS, and start_flush_worker's loop (:71-76) has no stop signal, never terminating. (d) crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/diagnostic_timeline.rs:226 classifies queue-full by `error.message().contains(\"queue is full\")`, a brittle string match rather than a typed error variant (this specific sub-item is elevated to important as AW-READY-O3, tracked separately -- this bundle keeps it at minor severity for the raw citation). Fix: ESCAPE clause or substr equality; document/assert bootstrap fragility; add a comment/assert for the silent OnceLock re-attach and a stop signal for the flush thread." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "retention-lifecycle" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T16:32:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AW2 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-05T16:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AW-READY-M8/aw-integrate-1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

# History (superseded by the in-place closure below, kept for narrative
# continuity): PR #1210 fixed (c)'s silent-discard half early; the
# flush-thread stop-signal half was tracked open through qa-pr1215 rounds.
# The LIKE-filter half (a) was fixed on fix/aw-readiness-easy@d9fa67fcc.
#
# quality-mgr, 2026-09-06, qa-phase-aw-integration-review-r2: closing the
# original integrate/phase-aw-linked occurrence in place. All four sub-items
# are now confirmed fixed at integrate/phase-aw@062cb44dd: (a) LIKE ESCAPE
# clause present (diagnostic_timeline.rs:92, ported from fix/aw-readiness-easy
# via merge-forward); (c) crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/diagnostic_timeline.rs
# now has an explicit stop_tx channel (start_flush_worker/stop_flush_worker),
# exercised by flush_worker_exits_when_it_receives_its_stop_signal, landed via
# 972f8eed3 (fix(readiness): stop diagnostic flush worker) and c5ff8b919
# (test(readiness): bound flush worker stop wait); the silent-discard
# OnceLock re-attach half was already fixed earlier via the AW-READY-O6
# idempotency guard (97c8ab886), same file; (d) queue-full classification
# moved to a typed error variant, tracked and closed separately as
# AW-READY-O3; (b) bootstrap AlreadyInstalled fragility remains an accepted,
# documented non-blocking fragility (not reachable in production, no fix
# required per the finding's own bundle framing). All fix commits are
# ancestors of integrate/phase-aw@062cb44dd. Independently confirmed by
# rust-service-hardening-agent and req-qa in the same review round.
